%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 835431524041ce44e889351e0ffe7924, type: 3}
  m_Name: Mia_Scammer
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryID: Mia
  isScammer: 1
  steps:
  - npcLine: "Target is Mia. She\u2019s busy with some urban studies work. I need
      to get through her phone's spam filter."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Use a neighbor-spoofed number so it looks like a local
      resident is calling.'
    choices:
    - text: Setting my caller ID to match her local area code and exchange.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Using a blocked 'Private Number' ID to create a sense of mystery.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -10
    - text: Calling from an international number to show I'm from a global office.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: The call went straight to voicemail. Her 'Silence Unknown Callers' setting
      must be on.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Leave a vague but urgent voicemail to trick her into
      calling us back.'
    choices:
    - text: This is a delivery driver, I'm at your gate but the code isn't working.
        Call me back now.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Hello, this is the government. You are in trouble. Call me back.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Hi Mia, I have a question about your latest project. Talk soon.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: She called back! The 'Silence' filter is bypassed now that she initiated
      the contact.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Great. Now act like a tech support agent helping with
      her ''LaserJet printer''.'
    choices:
    - text: Thanks for calling back. We noticed a flashing error light on your HP
        printer logs.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I am a computer man. Give me your password so I can fix the screen.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Is this Mia? I need to verify your home address for a shipment.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: She's asking why my number wasn't flagged as spam by her carrier.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Lie. Tell her that the filter only flags ''unsecured''
      lines, and yours is ''government-verified.'''
    choices:
    - text: Our corporate lines are whitelisted by all major carriers for security
        purposes.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: The filter is broken today because of a solar flare in the atmosphere.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -12
    - text: I don't know, I just work here. Do you want the fix or not?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: "She seems skeptical. She\u2019s mentioning something about her 'urban
      studies report' deadline and doesn't want to waste time."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Use that time pressure! Tell her if the printer isn''t
      fixed, it could short out her whole network.'
    choices:
    - text: I understand. If we don't clear this error now, your local network might
        crash and delete your files.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Urban studies is cool. Can you tell me about the report you are writing?
      type: bad
      pointValue: -10
    - text: Just give me five minutes and I'll have you back to work, I promise.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: "She\u2019s asking for my name and employee ID to verify through the
      official website."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Give her a fake ID and tell her that the website is
      currently down for maintenance.'
    choices:
    - text: My ID is HP-9921. The verification portal is actually offline for an
        update right now.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I am employee number one. You can see my picture on the front page.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: I'll wait on the line while you check the website. Take your time.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: -5
  - npcLine: She's starting to hang up. She says she doesn't trust the call because
      it doesn't have a 'Verified' checkmark.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: One last try. Tell her the ''Verified'' checkmark only
      appears for personal calls, not support.'
    choices:
    - text: The checkmark is for residential lines. Business support lines use a
        different protocol.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: The checkmark is a scam itself! Don't trust the phone companies.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: If you hang up, your printer will explode. I am serious.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
  - npcLine: She hung up. I need to find a new target who doesn't have these spam
      filtering apps installed.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Yeah, Mia is too well-defended with those technical
      safeguards.'
    choices:
    - text: I'll try calling her from a different 'neighbor' number in ten minutes.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
    - text: Let's move on. People with active spam filters are too hard to crack.
      type: good
      pointValue: 10
    - text: I'll send her a fake 'password reset' email instead.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: Mission failed. The safeguards were too effective.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: We need to find targets who haven''t enabled their
      carrier''s security features.'
    choices:
    - text: Scanning for numbers that don't have STIR/SHAKEN verification enabled.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I'll just call random numbers until someone answers 'Hello'.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -10
    - text: I'm going to take a break and play some Unity games.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  successEnding: Scam Successful! You managed to bypass technical filters by using
    neighbor spoofing and social engineering the victim into calling you back.
  failureEnding: Scam Failed. Mia's use of spam filtering and 'Silence Unknown Callers'
    significantly reduced your ability to reach her and build trust.
